# Trade records — personal financial data, never committed.
# daily_report.py reads these if present and draws nothing if not, so a
# checkout without them still builds every chart.
#
# These rules used to name the files: trades*.csv, *_fills.csv and so on.
# That was backwards. A broker export arrives called whatever the broker
# felt like -- 9-25-26_Robinhood.csv, 9-25-26_IBKR.xlsx -- and neither of
# those matched any pattern here, so the real files this tool was written
# for were the ones it would have let through. The listing is public.
#
# So the class is blocked instead of the names, and nothing tracked in
# tools/ is a spreadsheet or a CSV, so this costs nothing. Add an
# exception deliberately if that ever changes; the data files that DO
# belong in version control (notes.json and the two calendars) are JSON
# and are unaffected.
tools/*.csv
tools/*.tsv
tools/*.xlsx
tools/*.xlsm
tools/*.xls
tools/trades*.json
tools/*statement*
tools/*confirmation*
# Generated reports carry positions and P&L in the header.
tools/*.pdf
!tools/primer/SPCX_primer.pdf
